      "cannot_express": "A small crop, cheaply. Every region gets the engine's full 512x512 canvas whatever its source size, so a 45 px-wide region is upscaled 11x before it is diffused and the model invents the detail it finds there - the small-crop quality floor. Cost scales with the object count, so the number of objects becomes a frame-budget decision rather than a detection one; and each object is diffused with no sight of the rest of the frame, so nothing ties two objects' output together.",
